drafter.message_to_opposing_counsel:
Thank you for the first draft. We’ve made a light clean-up to bring it closer to market mutual-NDA form and to avoid ambiguity. The changes are intended to be non-substantive and should help both sides move quickly:

- clarified the agreement is mutual and applies equally to each party’s disclosures;
- defined “Confidential Information” more clearly and added standard exclusions;
- added customary compelled-disclosure language;
- added return/destruction and no-license provisions;
- aligned the remedy and survival language so the confidentiality obligations continue for the intended period after disclosure.

If helpful, we can also add a standard permitted-representatives provision in the next pass.
